{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And YHWH spoke to Moses.</b> The reason the passage is interrupted with the expression 'and He spoke' regarding the Day of Remembrance, the Day of Atonements, and Sukkot, is because each is a festival in its own right — unlike Shavuot, because it depends on the day of the waving of the omer, to count from there seven Sabbaths until Shavuot."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:37.524971298Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}